# Lab 6 — Work with Docs, Sheets and Slides — Generate, Review and Refine

**Topic 02:** Automating Work with Gemini Spark Tasks  |  **Day 1**  |  **Approx. 70 min**  |  **Course:** AI Agents with Gemini Spark (C1259)

> **Connected project:** this lab adds one more automation to the **Brightwave AI operations assistant** you began in Lab 1. If you fell behind, use the supplied Brightwave sample data to rejoin at this lab.

## Goal

Have the agent create a Doc, populate a Sheet and draft a Slides deck, then review and refine each output.

## What you'll build

A drafted Doc, a populated Sheet and a short Slides deck, each reviewed and refined once.

**Tools and techniques:** Google Docs, Google Sheets, Google Slides, content generation, structured extraction, review and refine

## Prerequisites

- Labs 1-5 complete.
- A few lines of notes to turn into a Sheet (or the Brightwave sample).

## Steps

### Step 1

Generate a Doc from a brief. Be specific about structure and length so it is easy to review.

Instruction to give the agent (paste into Gemini Spark):

```text
Write a 1-page Brightwave client onboarding checklist in a Doc: sections for Kickoff, Access, Brand assets, Timeline. Use checkboxes.
```

### Step 2

Review the Doc against the brief. Refine one section that is thin, then accept the version you are happy with.

### Step 3

Populate a Sheet from unstructured input. Give the agent a few lines of notes and a target column layout.

Instruction to give the agent (paste into Gemini Spark):

```text
Turn these notes into a Sheet with columns Client, Contact, Service, Fee, Status: <paste 4-5 lines of your own notes or the Brightwave sample>.
```

### Step 4

Open the Sheet and check every row parsed into the right column. Fix the instruction and re-run if a column is misaligned.

### Step 5

Draft a Slides deck from the Doc you made. Keep it short so review is quick.

Instruction to give the agent (paste into Gemini Spark):

```text
Create a 5-slide deck from my onboarding checklist Doc: title slide plus one slide per section, 3 bullets each.
```

### Step 6

Review the deck: is each slide on-message and uncluttered? Refine one slide, then keep the improved version.

### Step 7

Reflect on the pattern you just used three times — generate, review, refine — and note where it saved you the most time.

### Step 8

Save the Doc, Sheet and deck into your Brightwave assistant's Drive folder so later workflows can reuse them.

## Test it

You have a Doc, a Sheet and a Slides deck the agent generated, each reviewed and refined at least once, with the Sheet's data correctly placed in the right columns.

## Troubleshooting

- **The Sheet columns are misaligned.** State the exact column order and give one example row. Re-run; the agent maps to the columns you name.
- **The Doc is too long or off-structure.** Specify sections and a length ('1 page', 'checkboxes'). Refine the thin section rather than regenerating the whole Doc.
- **The Slides deck is cluttered.** Cap it: 'one slide per section, 3 bullets each, no paragraphs.' Review and refine one slide at a time.

## Challenge

Chain it by hand: generate the Doc, then ask for the Sheet and deck to be built from that same Doc so they stay consistent.

## Reflection

LO3 — The generate-review-refine loop repeated three times here. Where in your real work would that loop save the most time?

## Deliverable

Save your output — it becomes part of your **AI operations assistant**, the connected toolkit you consolidate, monitor and plan to scale in Lab 12.

